cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the reported results, please cite both the software and the paper."
title: "paper3 — Neuro-Symbolic Correction of Kazakh Word Forms (IHCONCS 2026 supplementary code)"
abstract: >
  Experimental code and reproducible results for the IHCONCS 2026 work-in-progress
  revision of "Neuro-Symbolic Correction of Kazakh Word Forms through Morphological
  Analysis and Contextual Disambiguation." Implements five measurable quantities
  (analyser coverage, candidate Recall@K, end-to-end P/R/F0.5/CER/WER,
  false-correction rate, risk–coverage) on top of the vendored kazmorph pipeline.
  No neural networks are trained here; the KazBERT POS/lemma checkpoints are
  restored from kazmorph-2026 and used for inference only.
